.recursive/STATE.md:8:- `/packages/pi-role-model/` provides the repo-owned Pi package for connecting Pi to an already-running Role-Model runtime. The public npm baseline is `@try-works/pi-role-model@0.1.0` for `pi install @try-works/pi-role-model`, while the current run 57 worktree package is `@try-works/pi-role-model@0.1.1` and includes compact taxonomy data, progressive group-first role/task classification, runtime taxonomy discovery with package snapshot fallback, and `role_model.intent` injection into real Pi provider requests for known Role-Model aliases. It ships a Pi manifest with `pi-package` metadata, `extensions/role-model.ts`, `skills/role-model/SKILL.md`, a single `/role-model` command dispatcher, typed external runtime discovery against `http://127.0.0.1:3456` by default, downstream OpenAI discovery parsing from `/api/role-model/downstream/openai`, compact `/v1/models` fallback, local-first endpoint trust checks, fail-closed auth-required handling, conservative Pi provider metadata mapping, `role-model` provider registration, Pi `setModel` alias selection, file-backed selected-alias state at `~/.pi/agent/role-model.json`, package-local tests, and install/setup docs. The package intentionally does not start the runtime, call the browser-opening launcher, copy credentials, run benchmarks, make hidden classification model calls by default, or read Pi auth files. Run 57 Phase 5 plus addendum 01 verified real local Pi package install/load/RPC commands/alias setup, six taxonomy-classified provider requests, and a live Pi prompt through healthy managed QA backends with telemetry showing `requestedRoleId=security`, `roleIds=[security]`, `ROLE_POLICY_APPLIED`, and `TASK_POLICY_APPLIED`.
